A student sorts the list [4, 9, 2, 7, 1, 6] in ascending order using this improved bubble sort:

def bubble(L):
    n = len(L)
    for i in range(n - 1):
        swapped = False
        for j in range(n - 1 - i):
            if L[j] > L[j + 1]:
                L[j], L[j + 1] = L[j + 1], L[j]
                swapped = True
        if not swapped:
            break
    return L

A 'pass' means one complete run of the inner loop.

